title: 'pallet-validator-collators: drop validators that author no blocks'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-validator-collators` can stop returning, for a number of Aura slots, validators that
    author no blocks within a number of Aura rounds. Governance sets the rule with the new
    `set_drop_rule` call. Without a rule, the default, nobody is dropped. The pallet counts the
    Aura slots between blocks, read from the Aura pre-runtime digest, and counts a gap longer
    than the Aura authority count as one slot. New storage items: `CountedSlots`,
    `CurrentDropRule`, `LastActivity` and `Dropped`. No migration.

    `pallet_validator_collators::Config` gains `AuthorityCount` (Aura authorities of the current
    session), which Asset Hub Westend and People Westend wire. External `WeightInfo`
    implementors must add `set_drop_rule`.
crates:
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-validator-set-announcer
  bump: none
- name: people-westend-integration-tests
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-zombienet-sdk-tests
  bump: none
